mode: "100644"
text: "# Lead magnets & funnels 2026 — verified\n\n*Volatile. Re-verify quarterly (formats/tools/benchmarks move).*\n\n## The dead playbook\nThe **2018 gated-PDF play** (10-page guide → email gate → 12-email blast) now pulls a fraction of its\nold leads. Two reasons: **AI assistants answer what PDFs used to** (no email required), and **ad-blockers\n+ email apathy** send most form-fills to spam/ignore. A \"12-page Ultimate Guide to X\" underperforms what's\npossible by **3–5×**. The problem usually isn't the funnel — **it's the magnet.**\n\n## What works now: interactive, instant, specific\n**Interactive / instant-result magnets** (quizzes, calculators, assessments, generators, specific\ntemplates) convert **~4× static PDFs**. **AI-personalized checklists ≈ 11.4% conversion-to-sale** in a\n30-day window vs **4.7%** for long-form PDF guides (CMI 2026 B2C report; attribute). The rules:\n- **One audience, one problem, one quick win** — relevance is the single biggest conversion lever; broad\n  = converts no one.\n- **Instant, on-the-spot result** (a score/plan/recommendation) beats \"check your inbox in 10 minutes.\"\n- **Quick to consume, easy to implement, immediately valuable** — minutes/hours, not days.\n- **Connects to the paid offer** — solves **one piece** of the larger puzzle so your product is the\n  complete solution (so it **qualifies**, not just collects).\n- **Specific, outcome-focused title** — e.g. \"The 5-Email Sequence That Books Discovery Calls.\"\n\n## Match the magnet to the funnel stage\n| Stage | Magnet | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Top** (cold, list-building) | quiz, calculator, mini-course | low friction, high volume |\n| **Mid** (engaged, qualify) | template, framework, benchmark report | higher commitment, qualifies |\n| **Bottom** (sales-ready) | case study, product ROI calculator, consultation/audit | converts intent |\nOne magnet for all three stages is why conversion suffers. **Templates that win:** specific-task (\"30/60/90\n-day plan\" not \"productivity\"), workflow-tied (Notion/Airtable/Sheets/Figma), industry-specific. **Original\ndata/benchmark reports compound for years.**\n\n## Design the WHOLE funnel (not just the magnet)\n```\nbenefit-first landing page -> short form -> instant success/thank-you page (sets expectations)\n-> delivery email (resends the asset) -> 3-5 email nurture -> soft next step toward the offer\n```\n- **Short form:** email (or email + first name) only — **each extra field cuts conversion ~5–10%.** Native\n  lead forms (Meta instant forms) = lower CPL but **lower quality**; landing pages = higher quality.\n- **On-page video** tends to lift landing conversion (the oft-cited \"up to 86%\" figure is a decade old —\n  treat as directional and A/B your own); **multi-step conversational forms +49.3%** completion.\n\n## The nurture (value-first, behavior-branched)\n**3–5 emails** is ideal (longer can convert even better): **deliver the asset → one quick win → proof/\nsocial proof → soft next step.** Skimmable, outcome-driven, links relevant to the magnet topic. **Branch\non behavior** (opens/clicks/page-visits), not just calendar drip. Don't pitch early — value-first keeps\nunsubscribes low. **Automated campaigns ≈ 2,361%** higher conversion than non-automated; **nurtured leads\n= 50% more sales-ready at 33% less cost**; **79% of leads never convert without follow-up.**\n\n## Economics + tools (advisory)\n**Create once, ~zero marginal cost per lead** (the 1,000th lead costs the same as the first). Tools (all\nexternal): magnet/quiz builders (Magnetly, Typeform), landing builders (Replo), ESPs (MailerLite/Mailchimp/\nSender/Kit), giveaways (Viral Loops/Vyper). **No dark patterns** — real value, honest proof, visible opt-out.\n"
